B4 is sent from the serial monitor (a line ending follows the command). For each blink the program switches the LED on for 150 ms and off for 100 ms. How many milliseconds does the blink loop take?

```
char komut = Serial.read();
if (komut == 'B') {
  int adet = Serial.parseInt();
  for (int i = 0; i < adet; i++) {
    digitalWrite(13, HIGH);
    delay(150);
    digitalWrite(13, LOW);
    delay(100);
  }
}
```

The LED should light when you send A from the serial monitor, but it does not. The monitor is at 9600 baud and the wiring is correct. Which line is wrong?

```
void loop() {
  if (Serial.available() > 0) {
    char c = Serial.read();
    if (c == 'a') {
      digitalWrite(13, HIGH);
    } else if (c == 'K') {
      digitalWrite(13, LOW);
    }
  }
}
```
